Package: SDLfilter
Type: Package
Title: Filtering and Assessing the Sample Size of Tracking Data
Version: 2.3.4
Date: 2026-11-26
Author: Takahiro Shimada
Maintainer: Takahiro Shimada <taka.shimada@gmail.com>
Description: Functions for filtering GPS and Argos tracking locations,
    visualising animal tracks, generating KMZ files, and assessing sample size
    for analyses of animal distributions. The filters remove temporal and
    spatial duplicates, fixes located at a specified height above the estimated
    high-tide line, and locations with high error, as described in Shimada et
    al. (2012) <doi:10.3354/meps09747> and Shimada et al. (2016)
    <doi:10.1007/s00227-015-2771-0>. Sample size for analyses of animal
    distributions can be assessed using the conventional area-based approach
    or an alternative probability-based approach, as described in Shimada et
    al. (2021) <doi:10.1111/2041-210X.13506>.
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0), ggplot2
Imports:
    data.table,
    dplyr,
    emmeans,
    geosphere,
    ggmap,
    ggspatial,
    gridExtra,
    lubridate,
    maps,
    pracma,
    sf,
    stars,
    utils,
    zip
